WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.381 --> 00:00:03.381
(audience cheering)

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:06.100
Wow!

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:07.966
It's kinda nice, huh?

00:00:07.966 --> 00:00:08.799
Yeah.

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:11.283
Yeah.

00:00:12.771 --> 00:00:14.496
You know, thanks so much for coming.

00:00:14.496 --> 00:00:15.974
[Audience Member] I love you!

00:00:15.974 --> 00:00:17.592
Oh, a guy loves you by the way.

00:00:17.592 --> 00:00:19.142
(audience member screams)

00:00:19.142 --> 00:00:20.374
Who is it, which one?

00:00:20.374 --> 00:00:21.818
(audience laughs)

00:00:21.818 --> 00:00:23.363
He's like, he thinks, No, me!

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:25.303
I have a chance now!

00:00:26.182 --> 00:00:27.015
(audience laughs)

00:00:27.015 --> 00:00:29.590
You know what, it's really nice,

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:31.150
I was so glad you could do the show.

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:33.250
I don't think, people don't know this,

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:35.630
but you were in the
audience at my audition.

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:37.210
Yeah, it was me seeing that tape.

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:38.610
Yeah, so you were at that.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:39.934
It was so nice.

00:00:39.934 --> 00:00:41.773
(audience awes)

00:00:41.773 --> 00:00:43.536
Don't mock our nice moment!

00:00:43.536 --> 00:00:45.349
Yeah, don't mock our real moment, yeah.

00:00:45.349 --> 00:00:47.970
No, but that was obviously
a big night in my life,

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:50.800
but we of course, best friends at the time

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:54.650
and you came and you sat in the audition,

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:55.953
sat through the whole thing
and told me you can do it.

00:00:55.953 --> 00:00:58.230
Through the whole thing, I know, ugh.

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:01.118
No, you were great, though.

00:01:01.118 --> 00:01:02.262
Oh well.

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:03.140
That was really funny.

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:04.280
Yeah, I looked all droopy.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:05.853
And what was I?

00:01:05.853 --> 00:01:06.760
Why didn't you, the
least you could've done

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:08.491
is say buy a real jacket.

00:01:08.491 --> 00:01:12.100
Don't use the Sears jacket
from your truck of your car.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.800
Remember we were trying
to make it not a big deal.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:15.410
Yeah, right, like it wasn't.

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:18.490
And you, at the time,
were going through a lot.

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:19.323
Yeah, I was.

00:01:19.323 --> 00:01:20.156
Thanks for bringing it up.

00:01:20.156 --> 00:01:21.483
I had gotten fired from Frasier.

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:24.210
Wait, what?

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:27.303
No, I just meant you
had a birthday recently.

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:30.990
(laughing)

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.080
I remember at the time
you were gonna do Frasier

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:34.910
and it didn't work out, the pilot,

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:35.743
and you were really upset

00:01:35.743 --> 00:01:36.640
and I said something better's gonna.

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:38.602
Remember, I said something
better's gonna come along.

00:01:38.602 --> 00:01:39.435
Yeah that's right.

00:01:39.435 --> 00:01:40.954
See ya, yeah that's right.

00:01:40.954 --> 00:01:41.787
(laughing)

00:01:41.787 --> 00:01:43.270
I gotta go to the Late Night Thing.

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:44.103
See you sucker!

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:47.050
But I said something
better's gonna come along

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:47.883
and then it did.

00:01:47.883 --> 00:01:49.180
Yeah, you were right.

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:51.099
I was just being nice.

00:01:51.099 --> 00:01:52.610
This whole story was about you were right.

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:53.470
Exactly!

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:55.220
All the stories should be about me.

00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:57.940
But you were really funny.

00:01:57.940 --> 00:01:59.810
Oh please, no please, let's not do that.

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:00.660
And now you set up straight

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:01.720
and now I sit like this.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:03.660
Yeah, I learned to sit upright.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:05.060
It took me seven years.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:06.400
And that was the whole key.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:08.580
Yeah, right, exactly.

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:09.530
I wanted to mention something.

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:11.290
One thing that a lot of people don't know

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:14.580
about you that I know because
we were friends for so long

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:16.500
is your special dessert that you whip up

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:20.360
for your good friends that
I want to share with people.

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:22.960
I used to live like three
blocks away from Lisa.

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:24.730
This is back in the early
days, we're struggling.

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:25.740
Lisa always used to call me up

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:27.420
and say I'm making my special dessert.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:28.860
Come on over and have some.

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:30.294
Her special dessert.

00:02:30.294 --> 00:02:33.294
(audience cheering)

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:38.330
That so depresses me, but anyway. I
know, what til you hear what it was.

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:41.810
So I'd come over and her special dessert

00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:44.160
was you would buy a big bag of M&amp;M's,

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:46.460
pour them on a tray, put
them in the microwave,

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:47.973
and melt it into goo.

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:52.110
I'm laughing because it wasn't goo.

00:02:53.007 --> 00:02:53.840
Yeah it was goo, yeah.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:54.673
You would just melt it into goo

00:02:54.673 --> 00:02:55.970
and you'd say it's an old family recipe.

00:02:55.970 --> 00:02:58.740
The microwave is like 15 years old.

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:00.230
How can it be an old family recipe?

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:02.430
Because it originated in the toaster oven.

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:05.423
Which goes back to the 15th Century.

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:07.640
Very nice.

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:09.240
Yeah, I understand
you're getting a little,

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:10.740
you've been irritated
lately with the tabloids.

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:12.010
Is that true?

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:12.843
Well a little bit.

00:03:12.843 --> 00:03:16.310
Not a huge amount, but you know,

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:18.130
they make things up.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:21.070
And I don't have it as
bad as other people do,

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:22.180
so that's okay, but you know.

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:24.900
They make things up about you, too.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:27.732
No, I have been in the
tabloids only twice.

00:03:27.732 --> 00:03:31.010
And both of my made-up
stories were so lame.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:32.070
Twice I've been in.

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:34.883
One was Conan O'Brien has
really high cholesterol.

00:03:36.056 --> 00:03:37.810
And they just cut out around my head.

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:39.010
You know when they just cut out your head

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:41.190
so your head's just floating.

00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:42.800
And they a picture like that.

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:46.290
And the other story was
they got a picture of me

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:48.510
just looking kinda confused or something

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:51.340
and they said Conan's pal says

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:54.427
he doesn't wash his hands
after using the bathroom.

00:03:54.427 --> 00:03:57.427
(audience cheering)

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:01.993
Yeah, so thanks, Andy.

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:07.703
You know, there's only
so much nagging I can do.

00:04:10.148 --> 00:04:12.980
I just always thought I want
a better story than that.

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:16.830
I want caught in love nest
with Gerry Ryan or something.

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:19.570
I know, make it something good

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:21.200
if you're just gonna plumb make it up.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:23.090
They said Courtney and I were seen

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:25.403
at Pea in the Pod Maternity Shop.

00:04:25.403 --> 00:04:26.236
Ah!

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:29.350
But we weren't, we weren't!

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:30.270
Yeah, but who cares?

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:31.820
That's not like a bad one.

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:34.680
I know, but why do they go
through the trouble to just,

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:36.279
you know, what can we do?

00:04:36.279 --> 00:04:38.127
(laughing)

00:04:38.127 --> 00:04:39.840
What do they think that's
gonna be really great?

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:41.290
I would love if a tabloid came out

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:42.360
and they just made up things

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:43.980
that weren't even that
interesting, you know?

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:47.430
Like Lisa Kudrow prefers
broccoli over carrots.

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:50.253
Exclamation point,
confused-looking picture of you.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:52.783
Broccoli next to you.

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:56.970
And life is good, everything's fine?

00:04:56.970 --> 00:04:58.240
Yeah, everything's really good.

00:04:58.240 --> 00:04:59.540
I see you all the time,

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:02.006
so I know your husband, Michel.

00:05:02.006 --> 00:05:05.390
Of course his family's from France.

00:05:05.390 --> 00:05:06.810
And I'm curious do they get the show,

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:08.110
do they get Friends over there?

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:11.280
Yeah, it's really big, it's
really, really big in France.

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:12.113
It's big in France.

00:05:12.113 --> 00:05:16.270
Yeah, so now most of his
relatives know who I am

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:18.090
and some of them just know.

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:20.460
This was the only thing I
didn't know how to take this,

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:21.990
some of them visited and then they left,

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:22.910
they called up Michel and said,

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:24.460
we had a really nice time, thank you.

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:26.560
And you know what, your wife got prettier.

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:30.160
Maybe that's a nice thing.

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:32.200
They weren't saying you
were a hideous ghoul before.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:33.050
See that's what I hear.

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:35.458
Oh see, well that's therapy.

00:05:35.458 --> 00:05:36.840
I hear she was a ghoul before and now,

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:38.770
thank god for you, lucky.

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:40.430
How do they show it in France?

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:42.675
Do they use subtitles?

00:05:42.675 --> 00:05:43.508
They dub it.

00:05:43.508 --> 00:05:44.341
Oh they dub it.

00:05:44.341 --> 00:05:45.204
They dub it.

00:05:45.204 --> 00:05:46.037
Well there's a cable.

00:05:46.037 --> 00:05:47.520
They show subtitles, that's the cool one.

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:50.320
And then on the network TV it's dubbed.

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:52.200
I think it would be so weird
to see yourself dubbed.

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:53.033
I've never seen that.

00:05:53.033 --> 00:05:54.620
But when you watch Friends dubbed

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.090
is it like, Well hello
Phoebe, how are you?

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:57.080
I am fine, Monica.

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:58.569
It's good to see you.

00:05:58.569 --> 00:05:59.402
Is it like that?

00:05:59.402 --> 00:06:01.700
I haven't really watched
it, I have to be honest.

00:06:01.700 --> 00:06:03.460
I've only heard about it.

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:04.500
You've never met any of the people

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:06.300
that have done the voices
or anything like that.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:07.740
No, but I've heard.

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:11.063
I've heard in Czechoslovakia,
there's one guy.

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:14.270
That's it for the whole show.

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:16.580
One guy does the voices
of everyone on the show?

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:18.870
At first I thought it was
one guy doing all the voices

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:20.763
and I found out he just narrates.

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:22.603
How do you narrate?

00:06:22.603 --> 00:06:25.130
So it's me talking like, Oh
Chandler, you're so floopy

00:06:25.130 --> 00:06:26.800
or whatever I would say.

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:30.849
And what is he translating to
the Czechoslovakian people?

00:06:30.849 --> 00:06:33.540
Oh Chandler, you're so.

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:34.990
I don't know what he's doing.

00:06:36.204 --> 00:06:38.020
Phoebe finds Chandler floopy.

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:39.410
Yeah, yeah.

00:06:39.410 --> 00:06:41.030
Phoebe just made up a word.

00:06:41.030 --> 00:06:43.604
Now she's leaving the
room and acting confused.

00:06:43.604 --> 00:06:45.205
[Audience Member] Phoebe!

00:06:45.205 --> 00:06:46.530
Very strange.

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:47.923
I'm just gonna be quiet.

00:06:49.641 --> 00:06:51.210
Yeah, stop making people yell.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:52.340
I'm sorry I'm making them yell.

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:53.906
Well we gotta go.

00:06:53.906 --> 00:06:55.460
Friends is of course, like
I have to mention this.

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:57.436
It's so funny, I'd better tell
people when Friends is on.

00:06:57.436 --> 00:06:58.530
Yeah, you better.

00:06:58.530 --> 00:06:59.820
Thursdays at eight o'clock.

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:01.010
Help that fledgling show.

00:07:01.010 --> 00:07:02.524
It's on NBC.

00:07:02.524 --> 00:07:03.357
(audience cheering)

00:07:03.357 --> 00:07:05.150
Lisa, thanks so much for coming.

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:05.983
So nice to have you.

00:07:05.983 --> 00:07:06.816
Lisa Kudrow, everybody.

00:07:06.816 --> 00:07:08.773
We'll take a break, we'll be right back.

